Unofficial Valgrind fork maintained by the hotpath-rs project
=============================================================

This is NOT an official Valgrind release and is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the Valgrind project. The official sources are at
https://sourceware.org/git/valgrind.git and https://valgrind.org/.

Fork: https://github.com/hotpath-rs/valgrind
Base: upstream tag VALGRIND_3_28_0 (Valgrind 3.28.0)
Version string: 3.28.0.hotpath2 (`valgrind --version`, Callgrind `creator:`)
Each release tag VALGRIND_<x>_<y>_<z>_HOTPATH_<n> matches the version
suffix hotpath<n> and is never moved.


License
-------

This fork does not change Valgrind's licensing. Valgrind is licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (see COPYING and the
README). The notice at the top of each file governs that file: most
allow GPL version 3 or any later version, some carry other terms (for
example the client headers include/valgrind.h.in and
callgrind/callgrind.h use a BSD-style license, and some imported files
are GPL version 2 or later). The documentation is covered by the GNU
Free Documentation License (COPYING.DOCS).

All original copyright and license notices are kept unchanged. The
hotpath-rs project claims no ownership of upstream code. Its
modifications, listed below, are contributed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version, and
each modified file carries a dated notice.


Distribution
------------

Every binary archive built from this fork contains COPYING, COPYING.DOCS
and README.hotpath, and names the release tag whose commit is its
complete corresponding source. Source archives made with `make dist`
include the same files.


Modifications
-------------

2026-11-01  VEX/priv/guest_arm64_toIR.c (arm64 guest, "B{L} uncond")

  An unconditional immediate B (without link) was given jump kind
  Ijk_Call, the same as BL. Callgrind therefore treated every plain B
  as a function call: each intra-function branch pushed a call frame,
  frames piled up (in loops, millions deep) until a real return unwound
  them, and inclusive costs overlapped. Symptoms: spurious recursion
  (`fn'2`) in non-recursive functions, including glibc's ld.so, and
  inclusive costs far above the program total. Exclusive (self) costs
  were not affected.

  Fix: B gets Ijk_Boring, BL keeps Ijk_Call. A B to the start of
  another function (a tail call) is still recognised by Callgrind's own
  jump-to-function-entry handling.

  Possibly related upstream report:
  https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=472460

2026-11-01  configure.ac

  Version suffix `hotpath1` (tag VALGRIND_3_28_0_HOTPATH_1), so reports
  from this build are never mistaken for, or compared with, an official
  3.28.0 build.

2026-11-01  README.hotpath, Makefile.am, configure.ac

  License section corrected to describe Valgrind's mixed licensing
  precisely; README.hotpath added to EXTRA_DIST so source archives carry
  it; version suffix bumped to `hotpath2` (tag VALGRIND_3_28_0_HOTPATH_2)
  because the source differs from VALGRIND_3_28_0_HOTPATH_1.


Building
--------

  ./autogen.sh
  ./configure --prefix=<install dir>
  make -j"$(nproc)"
  make install
